ory and elevated WBC, but LAP is typically low in reactive processes", "Myeloproliferative neoplasm (MPN) with atypical features: low hemoglobin/hematocrit contradicts classical CML presentation but remains in differential", "Diabetic metabolic decompensation: glucose 120 mg/dL and sodium docusate use suggest controlled diabetes, not acute crisis"], "alarm_features": ["Unexplained weight loss", "Marked leukocytosis with elevated LAP", "Mild hypercalcemia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.015, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP is more characteristic of CML than other myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPNs), which typically have low LAP. This finding adds moderate support for…"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.014, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP is more characteristic of CML than other myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPNs), which typically have low LAP. This finding adds moderate support for…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5203141339431191, "posterior": 0.5591287580899114, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP is more characteristic of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms like CML compared to reactive leukocytosis. This finding adds weak but meaningful s…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3", "B3.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "time_course", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia ver